{"id":"gotcha-example-001","type":"gotcha","fact":"Example: Truthy check on numeric values fails for explicit zero - if (value) is false when value === 0.","recommendation":"Use !== undefined or !== null instead of truthy checks when the value could legitimately be 0 or empty string.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"coderabbit","reference":"PR review","date":"2026-01-09"}],"tags":["javascript","type-coercion","validation"],"affectedFiles":["**/*.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"gotcha-hspec-match-zero","type":"gotcha","fact":"An hspec --match pattern that matches nothing reports 0 examples and exits 0, so a mistyped or too-narrow match silently 'passes'. There is no hspec-discover in this repo: a spec file missing from other-modules or either list in test/Main.hs never runs at all.","recommendation":"After every targeted `cabal test --test-options='--match \u2026'`, check the reported example count; treat a count of 0 (or a drop versus the previous baseline) as a failure.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"PR #283 (chat slash-command parity)","date":"2026-10-26"}],"tags":["testing","hspec","ci-gate"],"affectedFiles":["test/**/*.hs","seal-harness.cabal"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-10-26T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-26T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"gotcha-git-commit-am-new-files","type":"gotcha","fact":"git commit -am stages only modifications to tracked files; files created by the work unit (a new module and its spec) stay untracked while the local build stays green, so the commit ships a tree that does not compile for anyone else.","recommendation":"git add the new paths (and confirm `git status --short` is clean of `??`) before committing a work unit that adds a module or a spec.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"PR #283 (chat slash-command parity)","date":"2026-10-26"}],"tags":["git","workflow","commits"],"affectedFiles":[],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-10-26T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-26T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"gotcha-ws-conn-callback-closed-over-sid","type":"gotcha","fact":"Seal.Channels.Chat.Loop's WS event handler closes over the focused SessionId BY VALUE, so a FocusOp cannot re-target an existing connection: after /new or /tab focus the new session's SeEntry/SeAsk events are dropped (a plain turn's text arrives only over WS, so the session looks dead).","recommendation":"Carry the bound session alongside the client (WsConn = (SessionId, WsClient, StreamingState)) and rebuild the connection when the target changes. The obvious test ('a focus was recorded on the new sid') passes while the bug persists \u2014 assert a second connect, the old client closed, and an entry delivered through the NEW callback.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"PR #283 (chat slash-command parity)","date":"2026-10-26"}],"tags":["chat-channels","websocket","streaming","testing"],"affectedFiles":["src-chat-channels/Seal/Channels/Chat/Loop.hs"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-10-26T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-26T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"gotcha-mint-before-rebind-200","type":"gotcha","fact":"POST /api/sessions/:id/new mints the new session before it rebinds the tab, so a rebind failure must answer 200 with rebound:false plus the raw rebind_error: a 4xx would discard the id the caller needs for both the warning line and the confirmation line.","recommendation":"Keep the mint-before-rebind order, answer 200 on rebind failure, and pin the unreachable-by-HTTP branch through an extracted pure response builder (rebindNewResponse).","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"PR #283 (chat slash-command parity)","date":"2026-10-26"}],"tags":["gateway","api","sessions"],"affectedFiles":["src/Seal/Gateway/API.hs"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-10-26T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-26T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
